  "advice": {
    "leaf_rust": "This looks like coffee leaf rust. Remove and burn badly affected leaves, keep shade moderate so leaves dry faster, and ask the cooperative about a copper-based spray before the next rains. The extension officer has been informed.",
    "brown_eye_spot": "This looks like brown eye spot. It often comes with stressed or underfed plants. Check that the plants get enough fertiliser and some shade. The extension officer has been informed.",
    "leaf_miner": "This looks like coffee leaf miner. Pick and destroy leaves with brown tunnels. Do not spray broad insecticides that kill natural enemies; ask the extension officer first.",
    "coffee_berry_disease": "This looks like coffee berry disease on the green berries. Remove and destroy infected berries and talk to the extension officer about protective spraying in the wet season.",
    "berry_borer": "This looks like coffee berry borer. Pick up all fallen and dried berries, harvest ripe berries often, and ask the cooperative about borer traps.",
    "drought_stress": "This looks like water stress from dry weather. Mulch around the plants to keep the soil moist and keep some shade trees. The extension officer has been informed.",
    "nutrient_deficiency": "This looks like a nutrient shortage, often nitrogen. Ask the cooperative about fertiliser or compost for your coffee plants.",
    "unsure": "I am not sure what this is. I have sent your report to the extension officer, who will call you back. Please keep a few affected leaves to show them.",
    "no_input": "Sorry, I did not understand which signs you see. Please call again and describe the colour of the spots, where they are on the leaf, and if leaves or berries are damaged."
  }
